<title>UK: Halifax sets conversion vote date.</title>
<headline>Halifax sets conversion vote date.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-01-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Britain's Halifax Building Society, the country's biggest mortgage lender, said it would hold a special general meeting on February 24 to vote on its proposal to convert into a bank and float on the stock exchange.</p>
<p>In a brief statement saying that it had begun distributing its so-called transfer document to members, the society said its board &quot;strongly recommends that members should vote for conversion&quot; at the meeting.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
